[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248455808","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110209#issuecomment-3248455808","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110209","id":3248455808,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Bn4CA","user":{"login":"romgerman","id":1517367,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTczNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1517367?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman","html_url":"https://github.com/romgerman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-03T09:29:31Z","updated_at":"2025-09-03T09:36:11Z","body":"Edit: ok. I lied. It doesn't actually fix this. The inner class's method still doesn't get called. It does connect as far as I can understand, just doesn't get called by the signal. The inner classes are just broken when it comes to signals.\n\n<details>\n  <summary>My fix</summary>\n  \nFYI: temporary fix for signal connection is to delegate signal to the child node where inner class is instantiated\n```gdscript\n# my_child.gd\nextends Node\n\nsignal tick()\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n    get_parent().tick.connect(tick.emit)\n\tvar my_test = Test.new(tick)\n\tmy_test.try_connect()\n```\nthis way the signal is able to connect and call inner class's method and there are no memory leaks unlike when using a lambda as a wrapper for the inner class's method\n  \n</details>","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248455808/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248503810","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110209#issuecomment-3248503810","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110209","id":3248503810,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BoDwC","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-03T09:43:39Z","updated_at":"2025-09-03T09:43:39Z","body":"```gdscript\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tvar my_test = Test.new(get_parent().tick)\n\tmy_test.try_connect()\n```\n`my_test` exits scope after the end of `_ready` so it disconnects, you need to keep the object alive, try:\n```gdscript\nvar my_test\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tmy_test = Test.new(get_parent().tick)\n\tmy_test.try_connect()\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248503810/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248539207","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110209#issuecomment-3248539207","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110209","id":3248539207,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BoMZH","user":{"login":"romgerman","id":1517367,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTczNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1517367?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman","html_url":"https://github.com/romgerman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-03T09:54:23Z","updated_at":"2025-09-03T09:55:45Z","body":"> func _ready() -> void:\n> \tvar my_test = Test.new(get_parent().tick)\n> \tmy_test.try_connect()\n> `my_test` exits scope after the end of `_ready` so it disconnects, you need to keep the object alive, try:\n> \n> var my_test\n> \n> func _ready() -> void:\n> \tmy_test = Test.new(get_parent().tick)\n> \tmy_test.try_connect()\n\nYeah that could work for a simple use case like that but I'm making an EditorPlugin that is not that simple so I was trying to find a convenient way to fix this bug.\n\nI found a temporary fix **that works**. I moved my inner class into a separate GDScript file and it worked. Everything is connecting and freeing as it should. I don't know what's the matter with the inner classes at this point.\n\nPS. I don't know why the \"bug\" label was removed because in the MRP it clearly doesn't work as it should.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248539207/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248556681","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110209#issuecomment-3248556681","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110209","id":3248556681,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BoQqJ","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-03T09:59:39Z","updated_at":"2025-09-03T09:59:39Z","body":"This isn't a bug though, not as described, you are letting the object exit scope and it correctly handles that, unless the title of the issue is misleading and the issue is rather that connecting to a signal held in a local variable extends the scope of the containing class\n\nThe issues as described, i.e. \"connecting to a signal with a `RefCounted` that exits scope causes the signal to not trigger the bound method\", is not a bug but correct behavior\n\nThere's no reason the inner class should be kept alive here, so unless there's some specific detail I'm missing here I don't see what the bug is","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248556681/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248660204","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110209#issuecomment-3248660204","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110209","id":3248660204,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Bop7s","user":{"login":"romgerman","id":1517367,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTczNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1517367?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman","html_url":"https://github.com/romgerman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-03T10:28:08Z","updated_at":"2025-09-03T10:28:08Z","body":"> This isn't a bug though, not as described, you are letting the object exit scope and it correctly handles that, unless the title of the issue is misleading and the issue is rather that connecting to a signal held in a local variable extends the scope of the containing class\n> \n> The issues as described, i.e. \"connecting to a signal with a `RefCounted` that exits scope causes the signal to not trigger the bound method\", is not a bug but correct behavior\n> \n> There's no reason the inner class should be kept alive here, so unless there's some specific detail I'm missing here I don't see what the bug is\n\nBut then why inner class and a separate script class behave differently? Shouldn't they work the same way? (Correct me if they should work differently)\n\nThere are actually two problems but the main one is about signal connection. What's the difference between connecting an inner class method that exists a scope or connecting an inner class method wrapped in a lambda function? The second one works but the first one doesn't. And shouldn't the signal print an error if it's calling an invalid callable when it doesn't exist anymore? And the thing is if the object (inner class) is freed after exiting the scope, why it doesn't get freed when there is a lambda?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248660204/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248675311","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110209#issuecomment-3248675311","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110209","id":3248675311,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Botnv","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-03T10:33:03Z","updated_at":"2025-09-03T10:36:13Z","body":"How do they behave differently? There's no example code of a non-inner class for this that I can see\n\nLambdas do extend the life of some classes, in some cases that's a bug, the lambda lifespan is separated from the containing class in some cases due to limitations, I believe some of that has been fixed in 4.5, I will test that specific case in a recent version to see (this is still not working correctly as of 4.5, see https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102327)\n\n> And shouldn't the signal print an error if it's calling an invalid callable when it doesn't exist anymore?\n\nIt doesn't call an invalid callable though, the signal is disconnected when the class is freed, the inner class is never called because a class disconnects all signals targeting itself when it is freed\n\nBut to be clear:\nThe signal not being fired is as intended, otherwise a *lot* of engine functionality would break, if you want your object to persist you need to actually keep it alive in a variable","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248675311/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248786060","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110209#issuecomment-3248786060","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110209","id":3248786060,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BpIqM","user":{"login":"romgerman","id":1517367,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTczNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1517367?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman","html_url":"https://github.com/romgerman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-03T11:08:19Z","updated_at":"2025-09-03T11:08:19Z","body":"> How do they behave differently? There's no example code of a non-inner class for this that I can see\n\nYou are right. I was constantly changing my actual code (not MRP) to battle different behaviors that's why I stumbled upon total chaos.\n\nI remade MRP to show a different problem. It works as you described (the signal disconnects after the object is freed when leaving the scope). Until you add a reference to the parent class. Then it doesn't get freed at all. And I think that what confused me with the signal connection: one time I didn't have any references and the signal was disconnecting when an object was leaving its scope, next time I had a reference to the parent class and the object was never freed.\n\n[counting-references-or-something.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22116410/counting-references-or-something.zip)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248786060/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248793859","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110209#issuecomment-3248793859","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110209","id":3248793859,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BpKkD","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-03T11:10:57Z","updated_at":"2025-09-03T11:10:57Z","body":"Circular references are not supported, this is [documented](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_refcounted.html#class-refcounted)\n\nIs that the problems you are experiencing?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248793859/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248846531","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110209#issuecomment-3248846531","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110209","id":3248846531,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BpXbD","user":{"login":"romgerman","id":1517367,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTczNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1517367?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman","html_url":"https://github.com/romgerman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-03T11:28:55Z","updated_at":"2025-09-03T11:29:28Z","body":"I can't see anywhere in the documentation where it would state that signal doesn't hold a reference to a `Callable` and will disconnect when the `Callable` is destroyed (I guess that's why lambda worked and prevented the object from being destroyed). I think that was my problem.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248846531/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248867159","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110209#issuecomment-3248867159","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110209","id":3248867159,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BpcdX","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-03T11:36:16Z","updated_at":"2025-09-03T11:36:16Z","body":"We could specify that but I'd say that's the basic assumption that it doesn't, if it did that would break most code, it also does specify this at least partially in the [documentation](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_object.html#class-object-method-connect):\n> If the callable's object is freed, the connection will be lost.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248867159/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248886293","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110209#issuecomment-3248886293","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110209","id":3248886293,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BphIV","user":{"login":"romgerman","id":1517367,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTczNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1517367?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman","html_url":"https://github.com/romgerman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-03T11:43:03Z","updated_at":"2025-09-03T11:43:03Z","body":"That was my assumption with nodes but I didn't think it would work like that with all Objects because Nodes have their own quirks.\n\nIf you think that's enough of a notice you can close this issue. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248886293/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248896103","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110209#issuecomment-3248896103","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110209","id":3248896103,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Bpjhn","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-03T11:45:49Z","updated_at":"2025-09-03T11:45:49Z","body":"I think we could always add some further clarification, but the assumption is that the lifetime of a `RefCounted` is only as long as there are explicit references to it, it does in fact not work this way with `Object` as it doesn't do any lifetime management, that's specifically what `RefCounted` is for, `Node` doesn't get freed on its own but when it is explicitly freed, but other than that it all works the same, signals are disconnected when the object itself is freed\n\nBut we could add some note to clarify this absolutely, not sure how to phrase it clearer though","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248896103/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248985948","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110209#issuecomment-3248985948","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110209","id":3248985948,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Bp5dc","user":{"login":"romgerman","id":1517367,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTczNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1517367?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman","html_url":"https://github.com/romgerman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-03T12:10:26Z","updated_at":"2025-09-03T12:10:26Z","body":"I think https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102327 is the source of my confusion in this discussion and attempts to get my code working as it should. When I stumbled upon this behavior I assumed that the signal is connected as long as it exists (an object with the signal exists in memory, which was the wrong assumption) and not as long as a class instance with a connected method exists because I wrapped my method in a lambda and my object, instead of being freed, stayed in memory and the signal connection worked (which is wrong because it prevents the object from being freed until the object with the signal  defined is destroyed). \n\nSo yeah. Maybe the documrntation indeed needs a bit of clarification of why it works the way it does with different base classes such as  node, object, and refcounted. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248985948/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3248991854","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110209#issuecomment-3248991854","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110209","id":3248991854,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Bp65u","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_ur